  "notes": "{凝固|ぎょうこ} is a scientific term for a liquid becoming solid — used in both physics (solidification/freezing) and medicine (blood clotting).\n\nPHYSICS:\n- {凝固点|ぎょうこてん}: freezing point, solidification point\n- {融解|ゆうかい}: melting (opposite process)\n- {凝固|ぎょうこ}{熱|ねつ}: latent heat of solidification\n\nMEDICINE:\n- {血液|けつえき}{凝固|ぎょうこ}: blood coagulation\n- {凝固|ぎょうこ}{因子|いんし}: clotting factor\n- {抗|こう}{凝固|ぎょうこ}{薬|やく}: anticoagulant\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {固|かた}まる: to harden, solidify (everyday word)\n- {凍|こお}る: to freeze (everyday word for ice formation)\n- {凝固|ぎょうこ}: technical/scientific term for the same process",
